 ### Hash-based Value Noise
-A simpler 3D noise function using 1D hash interpolation and 3D trilinear interpolation of hash values at the 8 corners of the unit cube [S2, unofficial]. The algorithm defines $\text{step} = \text{float3}(110, 241, 171)$ [S2, unofficial]. It computes the integer part $\mathbf{i} = \lfloor \mathbf{x} \rfloor$ and fractional part $\mathbf{f} = \text{frac}(\mathbf{x})$ [S2, unofficial]. Smooth interpolation weights are computed as $u = f \cdot f \cdot (3.0 - 2.0 \cdot f)$ [S2, unofficial]. Finally, it performs 3D trilinear interpolation of hash values at the 8 corners of the unit cube using $\text{hash}(n + \text{dot}(\text{step}, \text{float3}(x,y,z)))$ [S2, unofficial].
+#### definition
+- [S2, unofficial] A simpler 3D noise function using 1D hash interpolation, often called Simplex-like or Value Noise.
+#### step
+- [S2, unofficial] Define `step = float3(110, 241, 171)`. Compute integer part `i = floor(x)` and fractional part `f = frac(x)`.
+- [S2, unofficial] Compute smooth interpolation weights: `u = f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f)`.
+- [S2, unofficial] Perform 3D trilinear interpolation of hash values at the 8 corners of the unit cube using `hash(n + dot(step, float3(x,y,z)))`.
